FFmpeg
------

vismod invokes the external `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` binaries at runtime
for video frame extraction. It does not bundle, link against, or
statically include FFmpeg — the Docker image installs it from the
distribution's package repository, and other deployments supply it on
`PATH`. Because the interaction is arms-length process execution over
files and pipes, FFmpeg's own license (LGPL or GPL depending on how the
build was configured) applies to FFmpeg alone and does not combine with
vismod's. FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard.


